.TH "bashclient\-api\-metadata" "5" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server file formats"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \f[B]api\-metadata.json\f[R] file is a machine\-readable API index
placed in the root of each client binding package directory (e.g.,
\f[CR]bash\-server/clients/python/api\-metadata.json\f[R],
\f[CR]bash\-server/clients/typescript/api\-metadata.json\f[R]).
It provides a complete, structured description of every public class,
method, type, error, and constant exported by that binding.
.PP
The primary consumers are \f[B]AI coding assistants\f[R] and
\f[B]tool\-discovery systems\f[R] that need to understand a client
library\(cqs API surface without parsing source code.
Human developers can also use it as a quick reference or to generate
documentation stubs.
.PP
Each binding maintains its own \f[B]api\-metadata.json\f[R] because the
public API surface differs across languages \(em Python exposes context
managers and async iterators, TypeScript uses Promises and generics, C
exposes opaque handles and error codes, and Java uses builders and
checked exceptions.
The file captures these language\-specific details while keeping a
uniform top\-level schema.
.SH FORMAT
The file MUST be valid JSON (RFC 8259).
All string values use UTF\-8 encoding.
The top\-level value is a JSON object with the following keys.
.SH Top\-level structure
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqpackage\(dq:   { \f[B]...\f[R] },
  \(dqmodules\(dq:   [ \f[B]...\f[R] ],
  \(dqclasses\(dq:   [ \f[B]...\f[R] ],
  \(dqtypes\(dq:     [ \f[B]...\f[R] ],
  \(dqerrors\(dq:    [ \f[B]...\f[R] ],
  \(dqconstants\(dq: [ \f[B]...\f[R] ],
  \(dqexamples\(dq:  [ \f[B]...\f[R] ]
}
.EE
.PP
All seven keys are REQUIRED.
An empty array \f[CR][]\f[R] is permitted where a section has no entries
(e.g., a minimal binding might have no custom types).
.SH package object
The \f[B]package\f[R] object describes the binding as a whole.
.PP
