.EE
.SH NOTES
The \f[B]api\-metadata.json\f[R] file MUST reside at the root of its
client binding directory:
.IP
.EX
bash\-server/clients/
  python/
    api\-metadata.json
    bashclient/
      __init__.py
      client.py
  typescript/
    api\-metadata.json
    src/
      index.ts
  c/
    api\-metadata.json
    include/
      bashclient.h
  java/
    api\-metadata.json
    src/
      ...
.EE
.PP
Validate the file with standard JSON tools:
.IP
.EX
python3 \-m json.tool api\-metadata.json > /dev/null
.EE
.PP
or
.IP
.EX
jq empty api\-metadata.json
.EE
.PP
The \f[B]version\f[R] field in the \f[B]package\f[R] object SHOULD track
the client binding version, not the bash\-server version.
When the bash\-server protocol changes in a way that affects the client
API, both the binding version and the metadata file should be updated
together.
.PP
AI tools consuming this file should treat the \f[B]signature\f[R] field
as the authoritative calling convention and the \f[B]parameters\f[R]
array as the structured breakdown.
If there is a conflict, the \f[B]signature\f[R] field takes precedence.
